Chapter 8. Unified Predictive Framework

Definition 2 (Megafire Prediction System). At each assimilation time t_k:

1. Prior ensemble: \boldsymbol{\theta}_{k|k-1}^{(i)} from the previous posterior via the transition kernel.
2. Update: \boldsymbol{\theta}_k^{(i)} = \text{EnSF\_update}(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{k|k-1}^{(i)}, \mathbf{y}_k) using the score.
3. Criticality index: R_f^{(i)} = \lambda(\boldsymbol{\theta}_k^{(i)})/(\mathrm{St}+\mathrm{Pe}^{-1}).
4. Megafire probability: P_{\text{mega}}(t_k) = \frac{1}{N}\sum_i \mathbf{1}_{\{R_f^{(i)} > R_f^*\}}.
5. Early‑warning: monitor \kappa(\hat g) from the empirical Fisher metric \hat g = \sigma^{-2}\hat J^{\mathsf T}\hat J.
6. Control decision: If an active fire exists and P_{\text{mega}}<1, solve the CLBF‑constrained optimal control to allocate \mu. If P_{\text{mega}}\to 1, declare uncontainability and shift to evacuation planning.

Conditional Correctness. If Propositions 2, 4, 6 and Conjecture 2 hold, the system correctly identifies the megafire boundary and prescribes safe control when R_f<R_f^*.

